hi everyone its Johanna here this is a  full six weeks weight training plan to  help you burn fat and to link up instead  of the traditional strength training  this workout plan is based on super  cells super sectioning are designed to  increase your heart rate increase your  metabolic rate and to turn the muscles  by decreasing the rest time between sets  one super cell has two exercises perform  10 repetitions per exercise do the two  exercises listed together with no rest  time in between and repeat the superset  for a total of 3 runs once they've  completed the first of all set move on  to the next superset with no more than  one minute rest in between  super sets short rest time will result  in greater calories burn and greater  after burn do this weight training plan  for six weeks to reduce your body fat  and to lean up so what you'll need is a  pair of dumbbells if you can choose two  pairs at two different weights one  lighter pair at two to four kilos each  and one medium weight at five to seven  kilos each this workout will only take  approximately 30 minutes to complete so  here are the exercises for Monday and  Thursday the muscles to focus on our  legs back and triceps superset one  dumbbell front squat and jumping lunges  dumbbell front squat stand shoulder  width apart with your toes pointed  forward gently rest a pair of dumbbells  just above your shoulders keep your body  upright and get your core and lower your  body as far as you can by pushing your  hips back and bending your knees then  drive with your heels back up to the  starting position and repeat tip your  knees should not go over your toes so  push your hips back jumping lunges stand  shoulder-width apart  and lunge forward with one foot jump  straight  as you throws your arms forward keeping  your elbows bent switch legs in mid-air  and learn in a lunge with the opposite  leg forward  super set to dumbbell plank row and  dumbbell row start in a push-up position  keeping your core tight balance your  weight on one arm as you pull the  dumbbell in the opposite hand up to the  side of your chest with your elbow  closed and pointer back squeeze your  back muscles lower the dumbbell and  repeat on the opposite side for  beginners you can start on your knees  tip keep your body straight by engaging  your core throughout the workout  dumbbell row keep your body upright  lower your upper body by bending from  your hips until it's nearly parallel to  the floor without moving your upper body  row the weights upward close to your  chest and squeeze your shoulder blades  together lower the dumbbells and repeat  superset three tricep dips and tricep  extension tricep dips place your palms  on the table chair or stepper with your  fingers pointed forward keep your legs  straight and body close to the chair  lower your body towards the floor by  bending your elbows hole for two counts  extend your arms raising your body  upwards and repeat for beginners you can  choose to bend your knees for an easier  option tricep extension hold one  dumbbell with both hands and lift it  over your head until both arms are fully  extended the palms of your hands should  be facing up toward the ceiling lower  the dumbbell as far as you can and  extend both arms straight up towards the  ceiling and repeat tip your upper arms  should remain stationary close to your  head throughout the workout and only the  forearms should move  super set for dumbbell deadlifts and  swimmer back extension dumbbell  deadlifts stand shoulder width apart  keep your body upright and dumbbells  close to your body slowly lower the  dumbbells past your knees by thrusting  your hips back and bend your knees drive  upwards through your heels pulling your  shoulders back and hips slightly forward  tip keep your head up and chest open  throughout the workout swim a back  extension lie on your belly face down  legs straight and arms extend it out in  front exhale as you lift your upper body  and legs off the floor pull for five  counts and squeeze your back muscles by  bringing your elbows close to the side  of your body inhale release and repeat  for Tuesday and Friday the muscles to  focus on our chest shoulders and biceps  superset one chest press and fly chest  press  lie on your back knees Bend and feet on  the floor bend your arms and keep the  dumbbells in line with your chest exhale  as you press the dumbbells toward the  ceiling squeezing your chest muscles and  keeping the elbows slightly bent inhale  lower the dumbbells to the starting  position and repeat fly lie on your back  knees bent and feet on the floor  keep both dumbbells together in line  with your chest with palms facing each  other as you inhale slowly extend your  elbows out to the side in a white arc  until your elbows touch the floor but  don't rest them exhale and return your  arms to the starting position by  squeezing your chest muscles superset to  show the press and up right row show the  press hold a pair of dumbbells with your  palms facing forward elbows banded and  the dumbbells in line with your ears  keeping your body upright throughout  press the dumbbells over your head lower  and  be careful not to arch your back by  engaging your core throughout the  exercise up right row stand  shoulder-width apart hold the dumbbells  with your palms facing the body use the  side of your shoulders to lift the  weights the dumbbells should be close to  your body as you move it up close to  your chin and your elbows should always  be higher than your forearms lower the  dumbbells back down and repeat superset  three bicep curls and arm circles bicep  curls stand shoulder width apart hold  the dumbbells with your palms facing  forward exhale curl both arms up  bringing your palms toward your biceps  inhale and uncurl back to the starting  position tip keep your elbows close to  your side throughout your upper arms  should remain stationary with only the  forearms moving arm circles extend both  arms out to your side palms facing up  keeping your elbows slightly bent make  10 small circles with your arms forward  and 10 small circles in the opposite  direction keep your arms extended to the  side and avoid dropping your arms down  superset for spider-man push-ups and  plank up down spider-man push-ups get  into a push-up position palms in line  with your chest slightly wider than  shoulder width apart as you lower your  body bring your left knee to your elbow  at the same time repeat on the other  side beginner start with push-ups on  your knees plank up down get into a  plank position by supporting your body  on your elbows and toes feet close  together arms 90 degrees with your  elbows directly under your shoulders  exhale and fully extend both arms into a  push-up position lower yourself back  down and repeat tip aim to keep your  body straight throughout with minimum  hate movement here are some additional  fitness tips breathing technique exhale  when you live the waves and inhale when  release always focus on proper form so  keep your body upright throughout the  workout by engaging your core muscles no  slouching do not rush the moves remember  nice and controlled movements not jerky  moves this workout is Peto proof as it  gets easier increase the weights use  increase the repetitions to 12 reps per  exercise increase to 4 rounds per  superset and decrease the rest time  between super sets if you stick by this  workout plan for the next six weeks eat  clean and perform twenty to thirty  minutes of cardio at the end of each  session I can assure you you will  produce your body fat and Lena all the  best for new fitness food and  motivational videos please like share  and subscribe to my youtube channel and  website do you follow me on Facebook  Instagram and Twitter to stay connected  with me thanks guys  you
 

